{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>From the fruit</b>, <b>death</b> — like [kaph]-[kaph], two gutturals that are adjacent."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra refers to the guttural letters kaph (כ) and kaph (כ) as identical adjacent letters in these two words; 'דבקים' means joined/adjacent."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:33.502492411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}